    {
      "id": "r20261121-a02",
      "title": "Why Jakarta Is Sinking",
      "level": "Menengah",
      "min": 3,
      "body": [
        "Jakarta is one of the fastest-sinking cities in the world. In some northern districts, the land goes down by up to 25 centimeters a year. Scientists say the sea could cover large parts of North Jakarta by 2050 if nothing changes.",
        "The main reason is underground water. Millions of people pump water from the ground because piped water is expensive or unavailable. As the water leaves the ground, the land above it slowly sinks, like a cushion losing air.",
        "The government is acting: it is building sea walls, planting mangroves, and moving the capital city to Kalimantan. But experts say the key step is simpler: give people clean piped water so they stop pumping. Saving the city will take decades, but every year matters."
      ],
      "gloss": {
        "sinking": "tenggelam",
        "districts": "distrik/wilayah",
        "pump": "memompa",
        "piped water": "air ledeng",
        "cushion": "bantal",
        "sea walls": "tanggul laut",
        "mangroves": "bakau",
        "decades": "dekade"
      },
